    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30-a16">

                <pb facs="0610" n="600" xml:id="pg600"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6599.3.1.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">“C”<lb/>(D.249–25.7.19) <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Military Mission</hi>, <placeName><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>[, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1919-08-06T15:30:00+01:00"
                            notBefore="1919-07-24T23:59:59+01:00">undated</date>].</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Haking</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armistice Commission Cologne.</hi></p>
                <p>I forward herewith a report by Captain T. Breen of this Mission, which is of
                    importance and seems to demand prompt action. Capt. Breen is making further
                    investigations, but looks upon this report as quite reliable. There is no doubt
                    that the Germans will make use of the period before the treaty comes into force
                    to dispose of as much property as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">N. Malcolm</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Major General,<lb/>Chief of British Military
                        Mission<lb/>1 Moltkestrasse, Berlin</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
